Subject: [PATCH] Open every sketch at 115200

Eight sketches, one constant each. Nothing else in this repo changes.

WHY. At 9600 the seventh strobe in a burst blocks the trial loop for 10-12 ms and
a 16-strobe burst spans 89 ms, against 7 ms at 115200 (docs/spikes/transport.md,
measured on a Mega 2560). Every emission a current task produces is depth 2, which
measures 0 ms at BOTH rates -- so this buys nothing today and buys an order of
magnitude of headroom before a task with more simultaneous strobes needs it.

115200 is the highest rate openable by generic POSIX tools: macOS stty rejects
250000 and above, so screen/minicom/cu cannot reach them, and losing
`screen /dev/cu.usbmodem... <rate>` as a 2 a.m. debugging path is a poor trade for
headroom the measurements say is unobservable.

READ THIS BEFORE APPLYING -- THE HOST MUST MOVE TOO.

A baud mismatch is not a clean error. It is a board that never answers, which
reads as a dead board: a mismatched console prints nothing legible rather than
reporting anything. Ephymeris' `defaultBaud` is a PERSISTED SETTING, so changing
its compiled default does not change a machine that already has a settings file --
someone has to set it in Config -> Hardware on each machine, or a box flashed from
this patch is mute until they do.

Task-Graph/docs/baud-rollout.md has the sequence, the full site inventory, and the
argument for not doing this as a flag day at all.

